   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Coal India subsidiary Mahanadi Coalfields Ltd (MCL) on Monday fixed a price band of ₹129-136 per equity share for its approximately ₹9,000-crore initial public offering (IPO), marking another major step in the government’s plan to list all Coal India subsidiaries by 2030. The IPO, entirely an offer for sale (OFS), will see Coal India offload around 66.2 crore equity shares, representing a 10% stake in its Sambalpur-headquartered subsidiary.",
   "summary_zh": "解锁这些内容需订阅 Coal India子公司Mahanadi Coalfields Ltd（MCL）周一为其约₹9,000亿卢比的首次公开募股（IPO）确定了每股₹129至₹136的价格区间，标志着政府推动到2030年将Coal India所有子公司上市的计划又迈出了重要一步。此次IPO全部为出售股份（OFS），Coal India将出售约6620万股普通股，占其总部位于 Sambalpur的子公司10%的股份。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Coal India subsidiary Mahanadi Coalfields Ltd (MCL) on Monday fixed a price band of ₹129-136 per equity share for its approximately ₹9,000-crore initial public offering (IPO), marking another major step in the government’s plan to list all Coal India subsidiaries by 2030. The IPO, entirely an offer for sale (OFS), will see Coal India offload around 66.2 crore equity shares, representing a 10% stake in its Sambalpur-headquartered subsidiary. The bidding window will open on November 19 and close on November 23. MCL produced 218.31 million tonnes (MT) of coal in FY26. It accounts for approximately 21% of India’s domestic coal production. The company operates 17 mines, including 14 opencast and three underground mines. MCL reported a net profit of ₹4,880.66 crore during the six months ended September 30, while revenue stood at ₹16,093.04 crore. The proposed listing is part of the government’s broader strategy to unlock value in Coal India’s subsidiaries through public listings and widen investor participation in the country’s coal sector. South Eastern Coalfields Ltd (SECL) and NLC India’s renewable energy arm, NLC India Renewables Ltd (NIRL), are also expected to make their stock market debuts during the current fiscal. coal / economy / business (general) / stock market / financial markets / iron and steel / mining Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
